# Maintenance Domain Foundation

This sprint introduced the **Maintenance Hierarchy** as the core domain model for the
maintenance system, not a feature specific to Maintenance Log V2. It is a shared
foundation:

```
Array
  ↓
Machine
  ↓
Component
```

Currently used by: Morning Round V2, Maintenance Log (V2), Maintenance Reports.

Future modules that will/should reuse it: Treatments, Annual Maintenance Plan,
BI/Analytics, KPI dashboards, Spare Parts, Maintenance History, and any other
maintenance-related feature.

## Rule: Do NOT duplicate this hierarchy

When implementing any new maintenance-related feature, reuse the existing
infrastructure instead of creating parallel tables, services, or lookup logic:

- **Arrays / hierarchy traversal** — backend: `MaintTrack.Application/Hierarchy/`
  (`IHierarchyService`, `HierarchyDto`, `HierarchyDefaults`),
  `MaintTrack.Infrastructure/Hierarchy/HierarchyService.cs`,
  `MaintTrack.Api/Endpoints/HierarchyEndpoints.cs`.
  Frontend: `frontend/src/services/hierarchyService.ts`.
- **Machine Components / mappings** — backend: `MaintTrack.Domain/MachineComponents/`
  (`MachineComponent`, `MachineComponentMapping`),
  `MaintTrack.Application/MachineComponents/` (`IMachineComponentService`, `MachineComponentDto`),
  `MaintTrack.Infrastructure/MachineComponents/MachineComponentService.cs`.
  Frontend: `frontend/src/services/machineComponentService.ts`.
- **Translation keys** for array/machine/component labels — reuse existing i18n keys
  in `frontend/src/i18n/translations.ts` rather than adding new ones for the same concepts.
- **Filtering logic** for Array → Machine → Component selection — reuse the patterns
  already implemented in `ReportsListScreen.tsx` / `MaintenanceLogV2Screen.tsx`
  rather than reimplementing selection/cascading logic per screen.

## Selection flow

- Selecting a machine → always go through **Array → Machine** using the hierarchy
  service, not a standalone machine lookup.
- Selecting a machine part → always go through **Machine → Component** using
  `MachineComponentService`/`machineComponentService.ts`, not a new/custom lookup table.

## When extending

Prefer extending `IHierarchyService`, `IMachineComponentService`, and their DTOs over
introducing new endpoints or tables that model the same Array/Machine/Component
relationships. If a new maintenance module needs data this hierarchy doesn't yet
expose, extend the existing service/DTO rather than building a parallel one.
